  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Intrinsic Asthma through a chain of indications that ultimately converge on Methylprednisolone, which in turn is linked to Intrinsic Asthma. This relationship is supported by the shared pathway where Prednisolone, through its indication of Chronic Primary Adrenal Insufficiency, Chronic Beryllium Disease, and Erythema Multiforme, all lead to Methylprednisolone, which then indicates Intrinsic Asthma. The low scores in all three paths suggest a weak but consistent association, possibly reflecting the indirect nature of the relationships. The mechanism appears to involve the use of Prednisolone as a therapeutic agent in conditions that are associated with Intrinsic Asthma, though the exact causal pathway remains unclear. The integration of these paths highlights a potential role of Methylprednisolone in the development of Intrinsic Asthma, though further research is needed to establish a definitive link."
